<section class="section section-soft"><div class="shell content-grid"><h2>Is this you?</h2><div class="content-body"><h3>You run a B2B company that already works. But money is still slipping through the cracks.</h3><p>Some sales never get followed up. People repeat the same work every week. Useful customer or sales data sits unused. You know there is a better way, but you do not want to fund another vague AI project.</p><p>The best fit is usually a founder-led company with about $1M–$20M+ in yearly revenue, 10–200 people and an existing customer base. It is an especially good fit when customers buy more than once.</p><div class="boundary"><strong>The key point</strong>You have a real business problem. AI is one possible tool, not the starting point.</div></div></div></section>
